@startuml
title Coder External Auth (OAuth2/OIDC) -> Token for Genetics API

actor Researcher as U
participant "Browser" as B
participant "Workspace\n(coder CLI)" as W
participant "Coder Control Plane\n(Server)" as C
participant "OAuth Provider\n(for Genetics API)" as OP
participant "Genetics Store API" as API

== Login to Coder (separate concern) ==
U -> B : Open Coder UI
B -> C : OIDC/OAuth Login (SSO)
C --> B : Session established

== First-time External Auth (Genetics) ==
U -> W : coder external-auth access-token genetics
W -> C : Request access token for provider=genetics
C --> W : Not authorized yet\nReturn "Open this URL" link

U -> B : Open External Auth URL
B -> C : GET /external-auth/genetics/start
C -> OP : Redirect to /authorize (client_id, scopes, redirect_uri, state, PKCE)
OP --> B : Login + Consent screen
U -> OP : Authenticate + Approve scopes
OP --> B : Redirect back to Coder redirect_uri\nwith authorization code + state
B -> C : GET /external-auth/genetics/callback?code=...&state=...

C -> OP : POST /token (code + verifier)\nexchange code for tokens
OP --> C : access_token (+ refresh_token, expires_in)

C -> C : Store tokens securely\nbound to user + provider

== Token retrieval inside Workspace ==
U -> W : coder external-auth access-token genetics
W -> C : Request access token (user=U, provider=genetics)
alt Access token still valid
 C --> W : access_token
else Expired
 C -> OP : POST /token (refresh_token)
 OP --> C : new access_token
 C --> W : new access_token
end

== API call ==
W -> API : HTTPS request\nAuthorization: Bearer access_token
API --> W : Response

note over C
Tokens are stored server-side (Coder control plane).
Workspace fetches short-lived access tokens on demand.
end note

note over API
To enforce "only from workspaces":
- keep API private (VPC / firewall / NetworkPolicy)
- optionally add mTLS / allowlist
end note

@enduml